Description: persistent console scrollback for Proxmox VE guests
 Keeps a log of a VM's serial console or a container's console from the
 moment the guest starts, whether or not a console is open, and replays its
 tail when the console is opened in the PVE web GUI, so it is no longer blank.
 Boot messages, kernel output, stuck shutdowns and link flaps that happened
 before you looked are still there.
 .
 Logging uses QEMU's chardev logfile option (via the VM's args) and liblxc's
 lxc.console.logfile. Replay wraps qm and dtach through dpkg-divert and only
 emits plain text and colour codes, so recorded cursor movement, screen modes
 and terminal queries cannot act on the live terminal. With python3-pyte the
 history is rendered through a terminal emulator first.

